ly for a community  center in a place that's that's needed  um so it's it's been a trying uh  situation one of the main reasons why  it's taking so long is because uh pastor  brooks has this vision  to build the community and center debt  free how much money do you have we have  about seven million allocated already  between pledges and commitments um so we  have a lot we still have a long way to  go another way that that kind of makes  it a little difficult as well  is is people um  they they want to see a finished product  before they sow into it ever since this  hotel has been knocked down 10 years ago  project hood has been grinding and has  been putting in the work we've had  construction classes we've had  entrepreneurial classes you don't have  to wait for the building to be built in  order for the work to begin the work has  already been done the building the  center is going to help us scale the  work that we're doing  america has really lost its focus  i mean we're always talking about racial  issues and racial divides  and we got these ideologies that are  constantly dividing us and splitting us  apart  where in reality  we are serving and we are here being  american citizens and that's what  america is really all about american  citizens coming together from all walks  of life  to see the issues that are going on and  coming up with positive solutions to  solve every problem that we face what  are you going to do about that so i'm  going back on the roof i mean if it  worked the first time let's try it again  so i'm going back on the roof but this  time i'm going to go for 100 days and  this time i'm not going to go by myself  i'm going to get some guests every day  some corporate figures some ceos and  presidents of companies the ceo  challenge where we are challenging ceos  from various companies to come and spend  the night with us join us in our efforts  to build this community center ken growl  is here the ceo of uptake uh data  analytic analytics company you you're  doing one night i'm doing one night  actually tomorrow night to kick it off  oh so you're one of the you're one of  the first uh  the guinea pigs  [Laughter]  i was at the  project hood golf outing uh up north  chicago and unfortunately the day got  rained out but  the pastor was gracious enough to stop  by everybody's table and introduce  himself and explain project hood in  greater detail  the idea behind the community center  and i was so intrigued and so inspired  by what he was trying to do and what  he's trying to accomplish and so for the  last  three weeks i've been trying to recruit  local ceos to come out here and join me  in camping out with the passer on top of  the  the roof here behind me who else is  going to be up there so we got kurt and  don bernanke curt is the ceo of related  management and don bernanke is the  president uh andy who is uh the  president and ceo of uh  sterling bay i believe that our  knowledge is limited and sometimes we  live in bubbles and the bubbles can be  in various different neighborhoods and  so  that gap for me is truly um unidentified  and that is a real reason why i want to  come here is to close that gap of  knowledge  [Music]  good job  these kids did not choose their mother  they did not choose their father  they were born in this area without a  choice  some of these people that are living out  here have never even left the confines  of this street  and so  what project hood wants to do  is to feel the void that they're missing  we're talking about kids that's never  seen a swimming pool we're talking about  young men and young women who want to  work  there's so much violence that goes on  and people don't know how to process  the deaths that are happening in their  families through gun violence we want to  have counseling and trauma centers and  all this stuff that is housed right here  we cannot put destiny in their hands  but this center will definitely put it  in their reach  [Music]  [Music